I’ll use the terminal app bundle to confirm whether `CopySelection` reaches the real application path, then I’ll resend the finding to `user-1` through Work Leaf.

The real terminal path does consume `CopySelection`: `TerminalAppCore::record_actions` queues it and `render_frame` emits OSC52. That makes the review item about the missing real-agent verification, not about the action being disconnected.

@work-leaf send user-1 Finding for commit 91cbd04dd75c79b6040aec4b2ead4830e1d257a0: [P1] Missing required real-agent verification for the terminal visual-mode feature. This patch changes terminal chat behavior: `src/ui.rs:464` binds visual selection entry (`v`, `V`, `Ctrl-V`, `Y`), and the real terminal path routes `CopySelection` through `src/terminal_app.rs:679` -> `TerminalUi::handle_key_with_content`, queues clipboard text in `src/terminal_app.rs:694`, and emits OSC52 in `src/terminal_app.rs:509`. The visible automated coverage I found is harness/fake-controller only (`tests/ui_harness.rs:578`, `tests/ui_harness.rs:594`, `tests/ui_harness.rs:607`, and `src/terminal_app.rs:1513`), while the ready message exposed only `@work-leaf done`. Because AGENTS.md requires real-agent verification for terminal chat behavior, please run/report a bounded real configured backend scenario: start the real Work Leaf terminal app with the configured Codex backend, create/select a real agent chat, exercise right-pane visual yank (`Ctrl-W l`, enter command mode, `v...y`) and left-pane visual yank (`Ctrl-W h`, `V...y` or block mode), and state the user-visible result such as the copied notice/OSC52 behavior. If Codex cannot initialize before `thread.started`, report the exact attempted command and pre-agent error, plus which automated tests cover the behavior.
@work-leaf done

